------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

these commands are how to use git whenever you're working

---------Switching branches----------------------------------------------------------------
git checkout (branch)           -> this switches the branch
ex.
git checkout main               -> switches your branch to main (where our main code is)

git pull
-> gets the latest code on that branch


---------Working on the project----------------------------------------------------------------
git checkout -b yourname/feature       -> this switches/creates a new branch on whatever your working on
ex.
git checkout -b rnaveee/creating-card-class

-> then work on your code
-> after you're done coding or want to save it to the branch:

git status                  -> shows you the files you changed
git add filename            -> add the file you changed to your branch
ex.
git add Card.h

git add .                   -> add all the files you changed

-> then run this to commit it to your branch

git commit -m "Message on what you changed"
ex.
git commit -m "Added card header files"

-> then push everything onto your branch
git push -u origin HEAD     -> pushes everything to your branch
or
git push -u origin yourname/short-description     -> pushes everything to your branch (does the same thing)

-> then make a pull request for me to review and put it into main
gh pr create --fill         -> makes a pull request

